cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Replicating emotion-concept vectors on Gemma-4-31B: circumplex geometry and control-prompt validation"
abstract: >-
  A replication of Sofroniew et al. (2026), "Emotion Concepts and their Function
  in a Large Language Model", which found internal representations of emotion
  concepts in Claude Sonnet 4.5 that causally influence the model's outputs. This
  work tests whether the finding transfers to an open-weights model, Gemma-4-31B:
  difference-of-means emotion vectors from the residual stream, a valence-arousal
  circumplex geometry check, and the cosine-similarity control-prompt validation
  that the earlier open replication omitted. Conditional on that validation gate,
  it further tests whether the model can detect the emotional direction it is
  being steered toward, and whether its misidentifications are graded in
  valence-arousal space.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Badilla-Olivas"
    given-names: "Antonio"
    email: antonio1dbo@gmail.com
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0000-6891-1562"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Antonio-Tresol/cbai-cambria-project"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - emotion vectors
  - activation steering
  - circumplex model
  - Gemma
  - AI safety
  - mechanistic interpretability
